111 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 68 0 R/T(Ileana Apostol is an urban scholar and architect whose work connects Zurich and Bucharest. Based in Zurich, she has been active in research and teaching in architecture, urban studies, and the politics of the built environment. Her Bucharest-related work focuses on urban memory, planning, preservation, and post-socialist city-making. Across both contexts, she links academic inquiry with civic and cultural engagement. Her work highlights the relationship between urban form, social justice, and historical change.)/E(Ileana Apostol is an urban scholar and architect whose work connects Zurich and Bucharest. Based in Zurich, she has been active in research and teaching in architecture, urban studies, and the politics of the built environment. Her Bucharest-related work focuses on urban memory, planning, preservation, and post-socialist city-making. Across both contexts, she links academic inquiry with civic and cultural engagement. Her work highlights the relationship between urban form, social justice, and historical change.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

