159 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 72 0 R/T(Kacper Pob\233ocki is an urban scholar working on class, inequality, and urban change in East-Central Europe. He holds a PhD in Sociology and Social Anthropology from Central European University and studied at University College Utrecht. His work has focused on urban movements, the right to the city, and the social transformation of Polish cities. He has long been involved in urban activism and co-organized the first National Congress of Urban Movements in 2011. He also co-authored A guide for the helpless: practicing the right to the city and is currently working on a book on urbanization and global economic change in Poland.)/E(Kacper Pob\233ocki is an urban scholar working on class, inequality, and urban change in East-Central Europe. He holds a PhD in Sociology and Social Anthropology from Central European University and studied at University College Utrecht. His work has focused on urban movements, the right to the city, and the social transformation of Polish cities. He has long been involved in urban activism and co-organized the first National Congress of Urban Movements in 2011. He also co-authored A guide for the helpless: practicing the right to the city and is currently working on a book on urbanization and global economic change in Poland.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

