331 0 obj
<</Title(Kacper Poblocki Anthropology)/Dest[9 0 R/Fit]/Parent 198 0 R/Prev 271 0 R/First 374 0 R/Last 374 0 R/Count -1/Next 375 0 R>>
endobj

332 0 obj
<</Title(Ileana Apostol Bucharest)/Dest[9 0 R/Fit]/Parent 198 0 R/Prev 375 0 R/Next 272 0 R>>
endobj

333 0 obj
<</Title(Ileana Apostol is an urban scholar and architect whose work connects Zurich and Bucharest. Based in Zurich, she has been active in research and teaching in architecture, urban studies, and the politics of the built environment. Her Bucharest-related work focuses on urban memory, planning, preservation, and post-socialist city-making. Across both contexts, she links academic inquiry with civic and cultural engagement. Her work highlights the relationship between urban form, social justice, and historical change.)/Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 273 0 R>>
endobj

334 0 obj
<</Title<>/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 275 0 R/Next 335 0 R>>
endobj

335 0 obj
<</Title(Historical urbanism, cultural work)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 275 0 R/Prev 334 0 R>>
endobj

336 0 obj
<</Title(Orhan Esen)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 275 0 R/First 376 0 R/Last 376 0 R/Count -1/Next 337 0 R>>
endobj

337 0 obj
<</Title(Justyna Orchowska)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 336 0 R/First 377 0 R/Last 378 0 R/Count -2/Next 276 0 R>>
endobj

338 0 obj
<</Title(Kacper Pob\233ocki is an urban scholar working on class, inequality, and urban change in East-Central Europe. He holds a PhD in Sociology and Social Anthropology from Central European University and studied at University College Utrecht. His work has focused on urban movements, the right to the city, and the social transformation of Polish cities. He has long been involved in urban activism and co-organized the first National Congress of Urban Movements in 2011. He also co-authored A guide for the helpless: practicing the right to the city and is currently working on a book on urbanization and global economic change in Poland.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 276 0 R>>
endobj

339 0 obj
<</Title(Dimitra Siatitsa is an urban researcher and planner based in Athens. Her work focuses on housing, urban development, and the politics of the city, with particular attention to social inequality and spatial justice. She has worked on urban governance, neighborhood transformation, and the everyday life of cities in the context of crisis and redevelopment. Athens serves as both her main base and a central reference point in her work.)/Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Parent 277 0 R>>
